{"id":"2qif3kb8ex23umyzncmlbpo","title":"Energy method approximation of small Laplacian deformations on Sobolev spaces","desc":"Energy-method proof that (−εΔ+1)u=f on a compact manifold gives a uniform-in-ε bound ∥u∥Hk​≤Ck​∥f∥Hk​ for every k≥0. Commuting powers of Δ through the equation and a coercive L2 identity yield the estimate; Sobolev embedding then extends it to the Xk=Hk∩L∞ norm.","updated":1763329309226,"created":1763329237773,"custom":{},"fname":"math.sobolev.energy-method-approximation-small-laplacian-deformations","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":".","selfContained":true,"name":"Dendron"},"contentHash":"6524a49c002db9430cd2eef5c0595918","links":[],"anchors":{"1-the-basic-l2-energy-estimate":{"type":"header","text":"1. The basic $L^2$ energy estimate","value":"1-the-basic-l2-energy-estimate","line":25,"column":0,"depth":1},"2-higher-even-derivatives-by-applying-powers-of-delta":{"type":"header","text":"2. Higher (even) derivatives by applying powers of $\\Delta$","value":"2-higher-even-derivatives-by-applying-powers-of-delta","line":41,"column":0,"depth":1},"3-from-deltascdot_l2-to-sobolev-norms":{"type":"header","text":"3. From $|\\Delta^{s}(\\cdot)|_{L^2}$​ to Sobolev norms","value":"3-from-deltascdot_l2-to-sobolev-norms","line":57,"column":0,"depth":1},"4-odd--arbitrary-integer-k":{"type":"header","text":"4. Odd / arbitrary integer k","value":"4-odd--arbitrary-integer-k","line":75,"column":0,"depth":1},"5-the-linfty-part-and-the-xk-estimate":{"type":"header","text":"5. The $L^\\infty$-part and the $X^k$-estimate","value":"5-the-linfty-part-and-the-xk-estimate","line":83,"column":0,"depth":1},"6-comments--why-this-is-cleaner-than-a-naive-energy-attempt":{"type":"header","text":"6. Comments / why this is cleaner than a naive energy attempt","value":"6-comments--why-this-is-cleaner-than-a-naive-energy-attempt","line":99,"column":0,"depth":1}},"children":[],"parent":"c7pgxpsgdxs4obnrs8eqena","data":{}}
